{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-14072","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-12729","text":"Runtime Walkthrough"}]},{"id":"blk-14073","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12730","text":"This page shows what happens when a runtime processes an "},{"id":"spn-12731","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/AmpersandBoxDesign/docs/architecture.md"}],"text":"`ampersand.json`"},{"id":"spn-12732","text":" declaration from start to finish."}]},{"id":"blk-14074","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12733","text":"The goal is to make the protocol operational, not just conceptual. The CLI flow shown here is reproducible in the reference implementation; for copy/paste setup steps and captured command output, see "},{"id":"spn-12734","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/AmpersandBoxDesign/docs/quickstart.md"}],"text":"`quickstart.md`"},{"id":"spn-12735","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-14075","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12736","text":"It answers practical questions such as:"}]},{"id":"blk-14076","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14078","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12737","text":"what gets validated first"}]}],"id":"blk-14077","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14080","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12738","text":"what gets normalized during composition"}]}],"id":"blk-14079","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14082","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12739","text":"when providers are resolved"}]}],"id":"blk-14081","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14084","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12740","text":"how governance and provenance are preserved"}]}],"id":"blk-14083","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14086","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12741","text":"what generation into MCP and A2A artifacts looks like"}]}],"id":"blk-14085","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14088","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12742","text":"what a failure looks like in CLI output"}]}],"id":"blk-14087","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-14089","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12743","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-14090","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-12744","text":"1. What this walkthrough is"}]},{"id":"blk-14091","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12745","text":"This is a "},{"id":"spn-12746","marks":["bold"],"text":"reference workflow"},{"id":"spn-12747","text":" for an implementation of the [&] Protocol."}]},{"id":"blk-14092","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12748","text":"It is not a requirement that every runtime use the same CLI syntax or internal module layout. It "},{"id":"spn-12749","marks":["bold"],"text":"is"},{"id":"spn-12750","text":" the intended lifecycle of the protocol:"}]},{"id":"blk-14093","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12751","text":"1. declaration 2. validation 3. composition 4. contract checking 5. provider resolution 6. generation 7. execution-time provenance emission"}]},{"id":"blk-14094","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12752","text":"In short:"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14096","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12753","text":"declaration → validation → composition → resolution → generation"}]}],"id":"blk-14095","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-14097","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12754","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-14098","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-12755","text":"2. A minimal declaration"}]},{"id":"blk-14099","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12756","text":"Consider an infrastructure operations agent that needs:"}]},{"id":"blk-14100","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14102","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12757","text":"graph-backed recall of prior incidents"}]}],"id":"blk-14101","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14104","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12758","text":"anomaly detection over telemetry"}]}],"id":"blk-14103","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14106","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12759","text":"fleet localization"}]}],"id":"blk-14105","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14108","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12760","text":"argument-based reasoning under governance constraints"}]}],"id":"blk-14107","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-14109","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12761","text":"A declaration may look like this:"}]},{"id":"blk-14110","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://protocol.ampersandboxdesign.com/schema/v0.1.0/ampersand.schema.json\",\n  \"agent\": \"infra-ops\",\n  \"version\": \"0.1.0\",\n  \"capabilities\": {\n    \"&memory.graph\": {\n      \"provider\": \"graphonomous\",\n      \"config\": {\n        \"instance\": \"infra-ops\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"&time.anomaly\": {\n      \"provider\": \"ticktickclock\",\n      \"config\": {\n        \"streams\": [\"cpu\", \"mem\", \"latency\"]\n      }\n    },\n    \"&space.fleet\": {\n      \"provider\": \"geofleetic\",\n      \"config\": {\n        \"regions\": [\"us-east-1\", \"us-west-2\", \"eu-central-1\"]\n      }\n    },\n    \"&reason.argument\": {\n      \"provider\": \"deliberatic\",\n      \"config\": {\n        \"governance\": \"constitutional\"\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"governance\": {\n    \"hard\": [\n      \"do_not_recommend_destructive_action_without_human_review\"\n    ],\n    \"soft\": [\n      \"prefer_reversible_remediation\"\n    ],\n    \"escalate_when\": [\n      \"confidence_below:0.75\",\n      \"cross_region_impact=true\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"provenance\": {\n    \"mode\": \"hash-linked\"\n  }\n}"},{"id":"blk-14111","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-12762","text":"What the runtime sees immediately"}]},{"id":"blk-14112","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12763","text":"Before doing any execution, a runtime can already infer:"}]},{"id":"blk-14113","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14115","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12764","text":"the declaration targets one agent: "},{"id":"spn-12765","marks":["code"],"text":"infra-ops"}]}],"id":"blk-14114","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14117","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12766","text":"four capability bindings are requested"}]}],"id":"blk-14116","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14119","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12767","text":"provider identity is explicit rather than automatic"}]}],"id":"blk-14118","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14121","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12768","text":"governance must survive the rest of the lifecycle"}]}],"id":"blk-14120","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14123","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12769","text":"provenance is expected to be preserved in a hash-linked form"}]}],"id":"blk-14122","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-14124","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12770","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-14125","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-12771","text":"3. Step 1: schema validation"}]},{"id":"blk-14126","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12772","text":"The first step is structural validation."}]},{"id":"blk-14127","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12773","text":"A CLI might expose that as (with reproducible command/output examples in "},{"id":"spn-12774","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/AmpersandBoxDesign/docs/quickstart.md"}],"text":"`quickstart.md`"},{"id":"spn-12775","text":"):"}]},{"id":"blk-14128","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"$ ampersand validate examples/infra-ops.ampersand.json\n✔ schema valid\n✔ agent id present\n✔ version present\n✔ capabilities object valid\n✔ governance object valid\n✔ provenance object valid"},{"id":"blk-14129","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12776","text":"At this stage the runtime is checking things like:"}]},{"id":"blk-14130","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14132","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12777","text":"required top-level fields exist"}]}],"id":"blk-14131","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14134","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12778","text":"the capabilities object is well-formed"}]}],"id":"blk-14133","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14136","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12779","text":"each capability entry matches the declaration schema"}]}],"id":"blk-14135","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14138","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12780","text":"governance and provenance fields have valid shapes"}]}],"id":"blk-14137","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-14139","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-12781","text":"What validation does not do yet"}]},{"id":"blk-14140","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12782","text":"Schema validation alone does "},{"id":"spn-12783","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-12784","text":" answer:"}]},{"id":"blk-14141","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14143","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12785","text":"whether the chosen provider really supports the capability"}]}],"id":"blk-14142","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14145","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12786","text":"whether capability combinations are semantically compatible"}]}],"id":"blk-14144","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14147","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12787","text":"whether a pipeline between operations is type-safe"}]}],"id":"blk-14146","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14149","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12788","text":"whether a provider can actually be launched in a target runtime"}]}],"id":"blk-14148","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-14150","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12789","text":"It only establishes that the declaration is structurally well-formed."}]},{"id":"blk-14151","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12790","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-14152","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-12791","text":"4. Step 2: normalization and composition"}]},{"id":"blk-14153","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12792","text":"After schema validation, the runtime normalizes the capability set."}]},{"id":"blk-14154","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12793","text":"This is where the protocol’s set-like semantics matter."}]},{"id":"blk-14155","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-12794","text":"What normalization typically does"}]},{"id":"blk-14156","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12795","text":"A runtime may:"}]},{"id":"blk-14157","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14159","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12796","text":"canonicalize capability keys"}]}],"id":"blk-14158","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14161","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12797","text":"normalize provider binding objects"}]}],"id":"blk-14160","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14163","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12798","text":"sort capabilities into a stable internal order"}]}],"id":"blk-14162","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14165","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12799","text":"collapse exact duplicates"}]}],"id":"blk-14164","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14167","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12800","text":"surface incompatible duplicate bindings as conflicts"}]}],"id":"blk-14166","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-14168","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12801","text":"For the declaration above, the normalized internal shape may be represented like this:"}]},{"id":"blk-14169","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"agent\": \"infra-ops\",\n  \"version\": \"0.1.0\",\n  \"capabilities\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"&memory.graph\",\n      \"provider\": \"graphonomous\",\n      \"config\": {\n        \"instance\": \"infra-ops\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"&reason.argument\",\n      \"provider\": \"deliberatic\",\n      \"config\": {\n        \"governance\": \"constitutional\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"&space.fleet\",\n      \"provider\": \"geofleetic\",\n      \"config\": {\n        \"regions\": [\"us-east-1\", \"us-west-2\", \"eu-central-1\"]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"&time.anomaly\",\n      \"provider\": \"ticktickclock\",\n      \"config\": {\n        \"streams\": [\"cpu\", \"mem\", \"latency\"]\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"governance\": {\n    \"hard\": [\n      \"do_not_recommend_destructive_action_without_human_review\"\n    ],\n    \"soft\": [\n      \"prefer_reversible_remediation\"\n    ],\n    \"escalate_when\": [\n      \"confidence_below:0.75\",\n      \"cross_region_impact=true\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"provenance\": {\n    \"mode\": \"hash-linked\"\n  }\n}"},{"id":"blk-14170","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12802","text":"The exact representation is runtime-specific. The important point is that composition produces a "},{"id":"spn-12803","marks":["bold"],"text":"deterministic, normalized capability graph"},{"id":"spn-12804","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-14171","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-12805","text":"Example CLI output"}]},{"id":"blk-14172","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12806","text":"The snippets below are illustrative of the same working commands demonstrated end-to-end in "},{"id":"spn-12807","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/AmpersandBoxDesign/docs/quickstart.md"}],"text":"`quickstart.md`"},{"id":"spn-12808","text":", where actual captured JSON output is included."}]},{"id":"blk-14173","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"$ ampersand compose examples/infra-ops.ampersand.json\n✔ normalized 4 capabilities\n✔ no duplicate bindings\n✔ no provider conflicts\n✔ governance preserved\n✔ provenance mode preserved"},{"id":"blk-14174","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12809","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-14175","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-12810","text":"5. Step 3: contract checking"}]},{"id":"blk-14176","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12811","text":"Once the declaration is normalized, the runtime can check capability contracts."}]},{"id":"blk-14177","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12812","text":"This is where the protocol moves from “well-shaped JSON” to “valid composition.”"}]},{"id":"blk-14178","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12813","text":"A runtime may verify:"}]},{"id":"blk-14179","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14181","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12814","text":"the capability subtype exists in a known registry"}]}],"id":"blk-14180","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14183","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12815","text":"the bound provider claims support for that subtype"}]}],"id":"blk-14182","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14185","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12816","text":"required operations are available"}]}],"id":"blk-14184","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14187","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12817","text":"declared or inferred pipelines are type-compatible"}]}],"id":"blk-14186","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14189","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12818","text":"adjacency rules such as "},{"id":"spn-12819","marks":["code"],"text":"accepts_from"},{"id":"spn-12820","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-12821","marks":["code"],"text":"feeds_into"},{"id":"spn-12822","text":" are satisfied"}]}],"id":"blk-14188","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-14190","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-12823","text":"Conceptual pipeline"}]},{"id":"blk-14191","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12824","text":"A common operational path for this agent might be:"}]},{"id":"blk-14192","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"stream_data\n|> &time.anomaly.detect()\n|> &memory.graph.enrich()\n|> &space.fleet.enrich()\n|> &reason.argument.evaluate()"},{"id":"blk-14193","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12825","text":"Important: "},{"id":"spn-12826","marks":["code"],"text":"|>"},{"id":"spn-12827","text":" is used in the docs as a "},{"id":"spn-12828","marks":["bold"],"text":"conceptual pipeline notation"},{"id":"spn-12829","text":". It expresses ordered flow between capability operations. It is not, by itself, a required wire format for the protocol and it is not required to be literal CLI syntax."}]},{"id":"blk-14194","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-12830","text":"What the runtime checks"}]},{"id":"blk-14195","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12831","text":"For that pipeline, the runtime asks:"}]},{"id":"blk-14196","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12832","text":"1. does "},{"id":"spn-12833","marks":["code"],"text":"&time.anomaly"},{"id":"spn-12834","text":" support "},{"id":"spn-12835","marks":["code"],"text":"detect"},{"id":"spn-12836","text":" 2. does "},{"id":"spn-12837","marks":["code"],"text":"detect"},{"id":"spn-12838","text":" emit a type that "},{"id":"spn-12839","marks":["code"],"text":"&memory.graph.enrich"},{"id":"spn-12840","text":" accepts 3. does "},{"id":"spn-12841","marks":["code"],"text":"&memory.graph.enrich"},{"id":"spn-12842","text":" emit a type that "},{"id":"spn-12843","marks":["code"],"text":"&space.fleet.enrich"},{"id":"spn-12844","text":" accepts 4. does "},{"id":"spn-12845","marks":["code"],"text":"&space.fleet.enrich"},{"id":"spn-12846","text":" emit a type that "},{"id":"spn-12847","marks":["code"],"text":"&reason.argument.evaluate"},{"id":"spn-12848","text":" accepts 5. do the adjacency rules permit each transition"}]},{"id":"blk-14197","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-12849","text":"Example success output"}]},{"id":"blk-14198","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"$ ampersand check examples/infra-ops.ampersand.json --pipeline infra_ops\n✔ capability contracts loaded\n✔ provider support metadata loaded\n✔ &time.anomaly.detect -> &memory.graph.enrich valid\n✔ &memory.graph.enrich -> &space.fleet.enrich valid\n✔ &space.fleet.enrich -> &reason.argument.evaluate valid\n✔ pipeline infra_ops is contract-safe"},{"id":"blk-14199","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12850","text":"At this point the runtime knows that the declaration is not only valid in shape, but also meaningful as a composed system."}]},{"id":"blk-14200","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12851","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-14201","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-12852","text":"6. Step 4: provider resolution"}]},{"id":"blk-14202","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12853","text":"Provider resolution answers:"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14204","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12854","text":"Which implementation actually satisfies each declared capability?"}]}],"id":"blk-14203","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-14205","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12855","text":"There are two common cases."}]},{"id":"blk-14206","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-12856","text":"Explicit provider binding"}]},{"id":"blk-14207","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12857","text":"In the example declaration, every capability names a provider directly:"}]},{"id":"blk-14208","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14210","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12858","marks":["code"],"text":"&memory.graph"},{"id":"spn-12859","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-12860","marks":["code"],"text":"graphonomous"}]}],"id":"blk-14209","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14212","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12861","marks":["code"],"text":"&time.anomaly"},{"id":"spn-12862","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-12863","marks":["code"],"text":"ticktickclock"}]}],"id":"blk-14211","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14214","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12864","marks":["code"],"text":"&space.fleet"},{"id":"spn-12865","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-12866","marks":["code"],"text":"geofleetic"}]}],"id":"blk-14213","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14216","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12867","marks":["code"],"text":"&reason.argument"},{"id":"spn-12868","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-12869","marks":["code"],"text":"deliberatic"}]}],"id":"blk-14215","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-14217","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12870","text":"In that case, resolution is mostly verification:"}]},{"id":"blk-14218","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14220","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12871","text":"is the provider known"}]}],"id":"blk-14219","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14222","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12872","text":"does the provider advertise support for this subtype"}]}],"id":"blk-14221","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14224","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12873","text":"are launch details or integration details available"}]}],"id":"blk-14223","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-14225","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-12874","text":"Automatic provider resolution"}]},{"id":"blk-14226","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12875","text":"If a declaration uses "},{"id":"spn-12876","marks":["code"],"text":"provider: \"auto\""},{"id":"spn-12877","text":", a runtime would consult a registry and select a provider that satisfies the requested capability and constraints."}]},{"id":"blk-14227","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12878","text":"For example:"}]},{"id":"blk-14228","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"&memory.graph\": {\n    \"provider\": \"auto\",\n    \"need\": \"relationship-aware incident recall\"\n  }\n}"},{"id":"blk-14229","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12879","text":"A runtime might then produce:"}]},{"id":"blk-14230","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"$ ampersand resolve examples/infra-ops-auto.ampersand.json\n✔ found 2 candidate providers for &memory.graph\n✔ selected graphonomous\n  reason: supports &memory.graph, mcp_v1 transport metadata present, graph recall operations available"},{"id":"blk-14231","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-12880","text":"About provider names in the docs"}]},{"id":"blk-14232","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12881","text":"Provider names such as "},{"id":"spn-12882","marks":["code"],"text":"graphonomous"},{"id":"spn-12883","text":", "},{"id":"spn-12884","marks":["code"],"text":"deliberatic"},{"id":"spn-12885","text":", "},{"id":"spn-12886","marks":["code"],"text":"ticktickclock"},{"id":"spn-12887","text":", and "},{"id":"spn-12888","marks":["code"],"text":"geofleetic"},{"id":"spn-12889","text":" are used throughout this documentation as "},{"id":"spn-12890","marks":["bold"],"text":"illustrative example providers unless explicitly stated otherwise"},{"id":"spn-12891","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-14233","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12892","text":"Their purpose is to make capability/provider separation concrete in examples. They should not be read as a guarantee that those providers currently exist as public implementations."}]},{"id":"blk-14234","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12893","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-14235","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-12894","text":"7. Step 5: generation into downstream artifacts"}]},{"id":"blk-14236","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12895","text":"After validation, composition, and provider resolution, the runtime can compile the declaration into downstream artifacts."}]},{"id":"blk-14237","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12896","text":"This is where the protocol becomes operational."}]},{"id":"blk-14238","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-12897","text":"7.1 MCP generation"}]},{"id":"blk-14239","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12898","text":"A generator may emit an MCP-oriented configuration that groups capability bindings by provider and preserves enough provider information for a tool-facing runtime."}]},{"id":"blk-14240","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12899","text":"An illustrative generated artifact might look like this:"}]},{"id":"blk-14241","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"graphonomous\": {\n      \"transport\": \"stdio\",\n      \"command\": \"graphonomous-mcp\",\n      \"args\": [\"serve\", \"--instance\", \"infra-ops\"]\n    },\n    \"ticktickclock\": {\n      \"transport\": \"stdio\",\n      \"command\": \"ticktickclock-mcp\",\n      \"args\": [\"serve\", \"--streams\", \"cpu,mem,latency\"]\n    },\n    \"geofleetic\": {\n      \"transport\": \"stdio\",\n      \"command\": \"geofleetic-mcp\",\n      \"args\": [\"serve\", \"--regions\", \"us-east-1,us-west-2,eu-central-1\"]\n    },\n    \"deliberatic\": {\n      \"transport\": \"stdio\",\n      \"command\": \"deliberatic-mcp\",\n      \"args\": [\"serve\", \"--governance\", \"constitutional\"]\n    }\n  }\n}"},{"id":"blk-14242","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12900","text":"A CLI could report:"}]},{"id":"blk-14243","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"$ ampersand generate mcp examples/infra-ops.ampersand.json -o build/mcp.json\n✔ generated MCP configuration\n✔ 4 provider entries emitted\n✔ unresolved providers: 0"},{"id":"blk-14244","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-12901","text":"Important constraint"}]},{"id":"blk-14245","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12902","text":"A generator should only emit details that are actually known from the runtime or registry metadata. If launch details are unknown, the artifact should preserve that explicitly instead of inventing them."}]},{"id":"blk-14246","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12903","text":"For example:"}]},{"id":"blk-14247","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"graphonomous\": {\n      \"transport\": \"unknown\",\n      \"status\": \"unresolved-launch-details\"\n    }\n  }\n}"},{"id":"blk-14248","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-12904","text":"7.2 A2A generation"}]},{"id":"blk-14249","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12905","text":"A generator may also emit an A2A-style coordination artifact or agent card."}]},{"id":"blk-14250","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12906","text":"An illustrative output could look like this:"}]},{"id":"blk-14251","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"agent\": {\n    \"id\": \"infra-ops\",\n    \"version\": \"0.1.0\",\n    \"skills\": [\n      \"memory.graph.recall\",\n      \"memory.graph.enrich\",\n      \"time.anomaly.detect\",\n      \"space.fleet.enrich\",\n      \"reason.argument.evaluate\"\n    ],\n    \"capabilities\": [\n      \"&memory.graph\",\n      \"&time.anomaly\",\n      \"&space.fleet\",\n      \"&reason.argument\"\n    ],\n    \"governance\": {\n      \"hard\": [\n        \"do_not_recommend_destructive_action_without_human_review\"\n      ],\n      \"soft\": [\n        \"prefer_reversible_remediation\"\n      ],\n      \"escalate_when\": [\n        \"confidence_below:0.75\",\n        \"cross_region_impact=true\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"provenance\": {\n      \"mode\": \"hash-linked\"\n    }\n  }\n}"},{"id":"blk-14252","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12907","text":"And the CLI might show:"}]},{"id":"blk-14253","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"$ ampersand generate a2a examples/infra-ops.ampersand.json -o build/agent-card.json\n✔ generated A2A artifact\n✔ 5 skills published\n✔ governance metadata preserved\n✔ provenance metadata preserved"},{"id":"blk-14254","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12908","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-14255","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-12909","text":"8. Step 6: runtime execution and provenance emission"}]},{"id":"blk-14256","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12910","text":"The protocol compiles declarations into downstream artifacts, but provenance becomes visible during execution."}]},{"id":"blk-14257","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12911","text":"Suppose telemetry enters the system and the runtime executes the conceptual pipeline:"}]},{"id":"blk-14258","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"stream_data\n|> &time.anomaly.detect()\n|> &memory.graph.enrich()\n|> &space.fleet.enrich()\n|> &reason.argument.evaluate()"},{"id":"blk-14259","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12912","text":"A provenance-aware runtime may emit records like:"}]},{"id":"blk-14260","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"[\n  {\n    \"source\": \"&time.anomaly\",\n    \"provider\": \"ticktickclock\",\n    \"operation\": \"detect\",\n    \"timestamp\": \"2026-03-14T14:23:07Z\",\n    \"input_hash\": \"sha256:1111aaaa\",\n    \"output_hash\": \"sha256:2222bbbb\",\n    \"parent_hash\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"source\": \"&memory.graph\",\n    \"provider\": \"graphonomous\",\n    \"operation\": \"enrich\",\n    \"timestamp\": \"2026-03-14T14:23:08Z\",\n    \"input_hash\": \"sha256:2222bbbb\",\n    \"output_hash\": \"sha256:3333cccc\",\n    \"parent_hash\": \"sha256:2222bbbb\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"source\": \"&space.fleet\",\n    \"provider\": \"geofleetic\",\n    \"operation\": \"enrich\",\n    \"timestamp\": \"2026-03-14T14:23:09Z\",\n    \"input_hash\": \"sha256:3333cccc\",\n    \"output_hash\": \"sha256:4444dddd\",\n    \"parent_hash\": \"sha256:3333cccc\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"source\": \"&reason.argument\",\n    \"provider\": \"deliberatic\",\n    \"operation\": \"evaluate\",\n    \"timestamp\": \"2026-03-14T14:23:10Z\",\n    \"input_hash\": \"sha256:4444dddd\",\n    \"output_hash\": \"sha256:5555eeee\",\n    \"parent_hash\": \"sha256:4444dddd\"\n  }\n]"},{"id":"blk-14261","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12913","text":"This is why provenance is treated as a protocol concern rather than as optional logging."}]},{"id":"blk-14262","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12914","text":"The declaration asked for provenance preservation. The runtime is now honoring that requirement at execution time."}]},{"id":"blk-14263","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12915","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-14264","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-12916","text":"9. What failure looks like"}]},{"id":"blk-14265","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12917","text":"A useful walkthrough needs at least one failing example."}]},{"id":"blk-14266","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12918","text":"Consider this invalid pipeline:"}]},{"id":"blk-14267","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"stream_data\n|> &time.anomaly.detect()\n|> &reason.argument.evaluate()\n|> &memory.graph.enrich()"},{"id":"blk-14268","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12919","text":"Assume:"}]},{"id":"blk-14269","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14271","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12920","marks":["code"],"text":"&time.anomaly.detect"},{"id":"spn-12921","text":" outputs "},{"id":"spn-12922","marks":["code"],"text":"anomaly_event"}]}],"id":"blk-14270","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14273","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12923","marks":["code"],"text":"&reason.argument.evaluate"},{"id":"spn-12924","text":" outputs "},{"id":"spn-12925","marks":["code"],"text":"decision_record"}]}],"id":"blk-14272","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14275","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12926","marks":["code"],"text":"&memory.graph.enrich"},{"id":"spn-12927","text":" expects "},{"id":"spn-12928","marks":["code"],"text":"incident_context"},{"id":"spn-12929","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-12930","marks":["code"],"text":"memory_context"}]}],"id":"blk-14274","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-14276","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12931","text":"The transition from "},{"id":"spn-12932","marks":["code"],"text":"&reason.argument.evaluate"},{"id":"spn-12933","text":" to "},{"id":"spn-12934","marks":["code"],"text":"&memory.graph.enrich"},{"id":"spn-12935","text":" may then be invalid."}]},{"id":"blk-14277","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-12936","text":"Example failure output"}]},{"id":"blk-14278","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"$ ampersand check examples/infra-ops-bad.ampersand.json --pipeline infra_ops_bad\n✔ capability contracts loaded\n✔ &time.anomaly.detect -> &reason.argument.evaluate valid\n✖ &reason.argument.evaluate -> &memory.graph.enrich invalid\n\nreason:\n  output type \"decision_record\" is not accepted by &memory.graph.enrich\n  allowed input types: [\"incident_context\", \"memory_context\"]\n\nexit status: 1"},{"id":"blk-14279","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12937","text":"That kind of failure is exactly why the composition layer exists. The protocol allows the runtime to reject bad compositions before they become runtime bugs."}]},{"id":"blk-14280","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12938","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-14281","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-12939","text":"10. What governance does during runtime processing"}]},{"id":"blk-14282","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12940","text":"Governance is declared early, but it influences more than one stage."}]},{"id":"blk-14283","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-12941","text":"During validation"}]},{"id":"blk-14284","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12942","text":"The runtime checks that governance fields are well-formed."}]},{"id":"blk-14285","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-12943","text":"During generation"}]},{"id":"blk-14286","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12944","text":"The runtime preserves governance metadata in generated artifacts so that downstream systems know what constraints travel with the agent."}]},{"id":"blk-14287","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-12945","text":"During execution"}]},{"id":"blk-14288","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12946","text":"The runtime or provider may enforce the declared constraints."}]},{"id":"blk-14289","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12947","text":"For the example declaration, a decision flow might produce:"}]},{"id":"blk-14290","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"$ ampersnad run examples/infra-ops.ampersand.json --input sample-event.json\n…\n! escalation triggered\n  reason: cross_region_impact=true\n  action: require_human_review"},{"id":"blk-14291","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12948","text":"The protocol does not require one universal enforcement engine. It requires governance intent to be "},{"id":"spn-12949","marks":["bold"],"text":"declared portably"},{"id":"spn-12950","text":" so runtimes can preserve and apply it consistently."}]},{"id":"blk-14292","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12951","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-14293","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-12952","text":"11. Reference lifecycle summary"}]},{"id":"blk-14294","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12953","text":"A compliant implementation should be understandable in terms of the following lifecycle:"}]},{"id":"blk-14295","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-12954","text":"Phase A: parse and validate"}]},{"id":"blk-14296","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14298","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12955","text":"read "},{"id":"spn-12956","marks":["code"],"text":"ampersand.json"}]}],"id":"blk-14297","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14300","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12957","text":"validate against the declaration schema"}]}],"id":"blk-14299","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14302","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12958","text":"reject malformed declarations"}]}],"id":"blk-14301","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-14303","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-12959","text":"Phase B: normalize and compose"}]},{"id":"blk-14304","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14306","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12960","text":"canonicalize capability bindings"}]}],"id":"blk-14305","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14308","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12961","text":"collapse exact duplicates"}]}],"id":"blk-14307","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14310","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12962","text":"surface conflicts explicitly"}]}],"id":"blk-14309","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14312","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12963","text":"preserve governance and provenance metadata"}]}],"id":"blk-14311","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-14313","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-12964","text":"Phase C: check semantics"}]},{"id":"blk-14314","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14316","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12965","text":"load contracts"}]}],"id":"blk-14315","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14318","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12966","text":"load registry or provider support metadata"}]}],"id":"blk-14317","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14320","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12967","text":"verify subtype support"}]}],"id":"blk-14319","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14322","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12968","text":"verify pipeline compatibility when applicable"}]}],"id":"blk-14321","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-14323","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-12969","text":"Phase D: resolve providers"}]},{"id":"blk-14324","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14326","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12970","text":"confirm explicit providers"}]}],"id":"blk-14325","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14328","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12971","text":"or select providers for "},{"id":"spn-12972","marks":["code"],"text":"provider: \"auto\""}]}],"id":"blk-14327","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-14329","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-12973","text":"Phase E: generate artifacts"}]},{"id":"blk-14330","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14332","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12974","text":"emit MCP configuration"}]}],"id":"blk-14331","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14334","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12975","text":"emit A2A coordination artifacts"}]}],"id":"blk-14333","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14336","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12976","text":"preserve unresolved details explicitly when they are unknown"}]}],"id":"blk-14335","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-14337","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-12977","text":"Phase F: execute with lineage"}]},{"id":"blk-14338","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14340","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12978","text":"run capability operations in the target runtime"}]}],"id":"blk-14339","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14342","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12979","text":"emit provenance records according to the declaration"}]}],"id":"blk-14341","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14344","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12980","text":"enforce or surface governance constraints"}]}],"id":"blk-14343","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-14345","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12981","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-14346","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-12982","text":"12. What is normative and what is illustrative"}]},{"id":"blk-14347","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12983","text":"This page includes both protocol expectations and implementation examples."}]},{"id":"blk-14348","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-12984","text":"Normative at the protocol level"}]},{"id":"blk-14349","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12985","text":"These ideas are central to the protocol model:"}]},{"id":"blk-14350","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14352","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12986","text":"declarations are validated before generation"}]}],"id":"blk-14351","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14354","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12987","text":"capability composition is distinct from execution"}]}],"id":"blk-14353","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14356","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12988","text":"provider identity is separate from capability identity"}]}],"id":"blk-14355","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14358","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12989","text":"contracts make composition checkable"}]}],"id":"blk-14357","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14360","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12990","text":"governance and provenance travel with the declaration"}]}],"id":"blk-14359","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14362","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12991","text":"downstream artifacts can be generated from a validated declaration"}]}],"id":"blk-14361","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-14363","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-12992","text":"Illustrative in this page"}]},{"id":"blk-14364","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12993","text":"These details are examples rather than mandatory:"}]},{"id":"blk-14365","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14367","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12994","text":"the exact CLI command names"}]}],"id":"blk-14366","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14369","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12995","text":"the exact terminal output format"}]}],"id":"blk-14368","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14371","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12996","text":"the internal normalized JSON shape"}]}],"id":"blk-14370","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14373","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12997","text":"the specific provider names used in examples"}]}],"id":"blk-14372","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14375","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12998","text":"the exact generated MCP command lines"}]}],"id":"blk-14374","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-14376","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-12999","text":"That distinction matters. The protocol defines the lifecycle and artifact roles, not one single implementation UX."}]},{"id":"blk-14377","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13000","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-14378","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-13001","text":"13. Why this walkthrough matters"}]},{"id":"blk-14379","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13002","text":"The most important idea in the protocol is not just that an agent can *declare* capabilities."}]},{"id":"blk-14380","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13003","text":"It is that a declaration can be:"}]},{"id":"blk-14381","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14383","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13004","text":"validated"}]}],"id":"blk-14382","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14385","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13005","text":"normalized"}]}],"id":"blk-14384","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14387","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13006","text":"checked"}]}],"id":"blk-14386","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14389","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13007","text":"resolved"}]}],"id":"blk-14388","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14391","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13008","text":"compiled"}]}],"id":"blk-14390","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14393","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13009","text":"executed with lineage preserved"}]}],"id":"blk-14392","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-14394","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13010","text":"Without that lifecycle, "},{"id":"spn-13011","marks":["code"],"text":"ampersand.json"},{"id":"spn-13012","text":" would be only documentation. With that lifecycle, it becomes an operational source of truth for agent composition."}]},{"id":"blk-14395","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13013","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-14396","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-13014","text":"14. Short summary"}]},{"id":"blk-14397","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13015","text":"A runtime processing the [&] Protocol should be understandable as:"}]},{"id":"blk-14398","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13016","text":"1. "},{"id":"spn-13017","marks":["bold"],"text":"validate the declaration"},{"id":"spn-13018","text":" 2. "},{"id":"spn-13019","marks":["bold"],"text":"normalize the capability set"},{"id":"spn-13020","text":" 3. "},{"id":"spn-13021","marks":["bold"],"text":"check contracts and pipeline compatibility"},{"id":"spn-13022","text":" 4. "},{"id":"spn-13023","marks":["bold"],"text":"resolve providers"},{"id":"spn-13024","text":" 5. "},{"id":"spn-13025","marks":["bold"],"text":"generate MCP and A2A artifacts"},{"id":"spn-13026","text":" 6. "},{"id":"spn-13027","marks":["bold"],"text":"emit provenance and apply governance during execution"}]},{"id":"blk-14399","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13028","text":"That is how the protocol moves from architecture description to runtime behavior."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierabru474fzjdtybnasytfbzlljw3s5ocokqu3sschnycwq6kn5ybga","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}